    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Voyage 34 is one of Porcupine Tree’s most distinctive early works, originally issued on Delerium Records as a long-form, instrumental ambient-electronic project split into four phases. Built around drifting synth textures, hypnotic rhythms, and spacey studio atmospherics, it draws heavily from ambient trance, space rock, and psychedelic electronic music, with Steven Wilson turning the piece into a continuous journey rather than a conventional song cycle.\n\nThe release became notable for its conceptually focused approach and its unusual length, presenting a narcotic, immersive sound world that stood apart from the band’s later more guitar-driven progressive rock. The material was later gathered and expanded as Voyage 34: The Complete Trip, which brought all four phases together in a single, remastered sequence and helped cement the piece as an early cult favorite among fans of Porcupine Tree’s more experimental side.",
